<title>RUSSIA: Russia tungsten exports fall, molybdenum soars.</title>
<headline>Russia tungsten exports fall, molybdenum soars.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia decreased its exports of tungsten and of articles made of tungsten over January-September by 36.4 percent to 208.7 tonnes, according to State Customs Committee data on Thursday.</p>
<p>In figures carried by Interfax news agency, September tungsten exports nearly doubled to 21.4 tonnes on August, with nearly 87 percent of deliveries going to Germany.</p>
<p>The committee said Russia nearly tripled its molybdenum exports over January-September to 465.3 tonnes.</p>
<p>September molybdenum exports were 20.4 tonnes, with nearly the entire total going to Germany.</p>
<p>The committee gave no absolute comparative figures.</p>
<p>-- Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
